\ Test that a catch inside the arm of a tail-position `if` reports no `if` row. The declared effect
\ makes the interpreter run the arm nested, so the `if` frame is still live when the catch folds the
\ chain.
\
\ Pinned to the interpreter. A compiled `recover` inlined into an arm leaves out its own row, which
\ is a separate gap.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "boom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;

caught-in-arm: ( ? -- ) [ [ ( -- ) [ boom ] [ inspect print-line ] recover ] [ ] if ] ;

t caught-in-arm
